{"ts":"2026-05-12T18:25:44.847Z","event":"bd_exec","request_id":"c6eb9156-0744-4a3a-9972-9dadb3f5bb96","argv":["--json","create","In extensions/lib/mode-prompts.ts around lines 12-35 (top, near buildCommanderSection), add a new exported helper buildDelegateEverythingSection(opts: ModePromptOpts): string that returns the unconditional Main-Agent-as-Planner policy block; this becomes the single source of truth all mode prompts import — the section must (1) state explicitly that the main agent does ONLY thinking, planning, synthesis, user-facing response, and orchestration tool calls, (2) forbid Read/Bash/Grep/Glob/Edit/Write/run-tests/run-builds/git etc. by the main agent — these route to subagents via subagent_create/subagent_create_batch/dispatch_agent/run_chain depending on mode, (3) enumerate the allowed orchestration toolset (subagent_*, dispatch_agent, run_chain, set_mode, show_plan, show_spec, show_report, ask_user, tasks, commander_*, complex_problem_loop_*), (4) include guidance that when a pre-spawned scout exists (opts.scoutId != null) the agent SHOULD use subagent_continue against it, but absence of a scout is NOT a permission to act directly — spawn one on demand, (5) call out batching reads to amortize subagent spawn cost, (6) include the 'do not even use Bash for tests/builds' explicit clause to prevent regression of the prior TEAM carve-out. Do NOT yet wire it into mode builders — that happens in dependent tasks.","-d","In extensions/lib/mode-prompts.ts around lines 12-35 (top, near buildCommanderSection), add a new exported helper buildDelegateEverythingSection(opts: ModePromptOpts): string that returns the unconditional Main-Agent-as-Planner policy block; this becomes the single source of truth all mode prompts import — the section must (1) state explicitly that the main agent does ONLY thinking, planning, synthesis, user-facing response, and orchestration tool calls, (2) forbid Read/Bash/Grep/Glob/Edit/Write/run-tests/run-builds/git etc. by the main